    <info>
        <title><package>man-pages</package> update strategy</title>
        <meta name="maintainer" content="daria.vladykina@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
        <abstract>
            <para>The <package>man-pages</package> package provides the primary reference documentation for 
                Linux system calls, C library functions, device files, file formats and system administration 
                conventions.</para>
        </abstract>
    </info>
    <para>
        The <package>man-pages</package> package follows the balanced lifecycle model across all 
        &suselinux;&nbsp;16 codestreams. The package is updated according to the following rules:
    </para>
    
    <variablelist xml:id="vlist-man-rules">
        <varlistentry>
            <term>Lifecycle model</term>
            <listitem>
                <para>Balanced</para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term>Minor release synchronization</term>
            <listitem><para>
                    With each new &suselinux;&nbsp;16 minor release, <package>man-pages</package> is 
                    updated to the latest upstream version.</para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>
        <varlistentry>
            <term>Kernel and API alignment</term>
            <listitem>
                <para>The primary objective of these periodic version updates is to ensure system 
                    documentation stays in sync with new kernel updates, system call modifications 
                    and C library (<package>glibc</package>) enhancements introduced in each minor release.</para>
            </listitem>
        </varlistentry>        
    </variablelist>
</topic>
